Yes machan 👍 You have now covered **C++ Vector** and **Java ArrayList**. Let's add **Python List** to the same notes so you can compare all three languages.

The important mapping is:

| Concept       | C++                              | Java              | Python                        |
| ------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------- | ----------------------------- |
| Dynamic array | `vector`                         | `ArrayList`       | `list`                        |
| Add at end    | `push_back()` / `emplace_back()` | `add()`           | `append()`                    |
| Access        | `v[index]`                       | `list.get(index)` | `list[index]`                 |
| Modify        | `v[index] = x`                   | `set(index, x)`   | `list[index] = x`             |
| Insert        | `insert()`                       | `add(index, x)`   | `insert(index, x)`            |
| Remove        | `erase()`                        | `remove()`        | `remove()` / `pop()`          |
| Size          | `size()`                         | `size()`          | `len()`                       |
| Clear         | `clear()`                        | `clear()`         | `clear()`                     |
| Empty         | `empty()`                        | `isEmpty()`       | `not list` / `len(list) == 0` |

